     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Because there are seven digits in 4,130,045, <i>n</i> is 7. So, start with the first digit (4) times 10 raised to <i>n</i> – 1, which is the sixth power.</p>\n<p>Add the next digit times 10 raised to one less than the previous power.</p>\n<p>Continue until you end with the last digit times 10<sup>0</sup>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"4 \\times {10^6} + 1 \\times {10^5} + 3 \\times {10^4} + 0 \\times {10^3} + 0 \\times {10^2} + 4 \\times {10^1} + 5 \\times {10^0}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"4 \\times {10^6} + 1 \\times {10^5} + 3 \\times {10^4} + 0 \\times {10^3} + 0 \\times {10^2} + 4 \\times {10^1} + 5 \\times {10^0}\">4 \\times {10^6} + 1 \\times {10^5} + 3 \\times {10^4} + 0 \\times {10^3} + 0 \\times {10^2} + 4 \\times {10^1} + 5 \\times {10^0}</span>"
